:: Carter Hero Award Intro [nobr]

/* Intro */
English class is as you expect, <span style="Color: Yellow">boring and a struggle to stay awake.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mr. Hart</span> had tried to give a lecture about themes and settings and all the buzz words that come with reading but had given up once his sleepiness had caused him to lose his train of thought. He now stood by the coffee machine waiting impatiently as everyone else does worksheets about what he tried to teach. You are doodling on the corner of your worksheet trying to pass the time <span style="Color: Yellow">when, much to everyone’s surprise, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Headmaster Alistair</span> walks in.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Alistair",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Uniform",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hello, sorry to disturb but I was wondering if I could borrow <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter Kent</span> for a second? I need to speak with him in my office.”</span> He says, causing all eyes to instantly spin towards <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, the classic array of <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ooo, he’s in trouble!”</span> that come with being called to the principal’s office fill the room. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> assures the class that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> isn’t in any kind of trouble, but the small boy does blush and looks a little nervous as he follows him out. He glances towards you briefly before leaving and you give him a reassuring smile. <span style="Color: Yellow">You’re sure it’s nothing, though still can’t but feel very curious.</span> <br>
<br>
Class continues as expected, once he has his coffee in him, Mr. Hart tries to resume the lecture, though now finds himself more than a little jittery and has some trouble focusing, eventually going on a long rant about his distaste for a certain author of wizard books. He makes some good points, though you can hardly focus on it as your mind ponders what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> could be dealing with. <span style="Color: Yellow">He has been gone nearly 20 minutes when the door to the classroom opens again, however, it isn’t <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> or <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Headmaster Alistair</span>, but rather the school’s secretary.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 1,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, I was wondering if I could steal <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name $Player.LastName</span> for a minute?”</span> She asks Mr. Hart and just like that, the same eyes and teasing words that were on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> now fall on you. You blush and stand up, grabbing your things as you follow the secretary out into the hallway. <span style="Color: Yellow">You feel your face flush and your brain start spinning with all the possible reasons you could be getting called to the office and how <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> fits into it. Your heart is racing by the time you reach the front and walk in.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    You are led through the main office towards the Headmaster’s Office. As you pass by, you spy <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> off to the side, talking on the phone as he seems to whip his eyes with tissues! <span style="Color: Yellow">You can’t see his face, but you have no doubt that he has been crying by the slight tremble in his voice and the dampness of the tissues! Your worry grows 10-fold as you step into the office and sit down, worried out of your mind as you stare up at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span>, who types something on his computer with a serious expression.</span> <br>
    <br>
    You are sitting there for about a minute before <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> seems to notice you, his face snapping back to reality as if he was lost in thought. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>!”</span> He smiles, which briefly calms your nerves, though your fear must still be clear on your face. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Why do you look so-? Oh, I see.”</span> He laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This is one of those good headmaster’s office visits, trust me, no need to look so scared.”</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You feel a weight lifted off your chest as he assures you that you aren’t in any trouble,</span> though you glance over to the door, wondering why <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> seemed upset. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> will be back in just a second; the little guy just got a little overwhelmed.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I often work with the city for various projects and one thing me and the other schools in the district have been working on is a new annual awards ceremony meant to commend those who give back to the community. It’s meant to promote goodwill and charity. Each school nominates one student known for good deeds and selflessness to receive an award.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> explains. You start to piece together what’s happening, guessing that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> won the award for this school. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Huh? Oh, no, a third year is our nominee.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> replies, leaving you more confused. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But there is an additional award, called the Hero Award. Nominated by the city itself for those that show a truly selfless spirit and go above and beyond for their community.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> smiles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That is what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is be awarded. The board was supposed to come up with a few nominees for us to evaluate and choose, but everyone had the same person in mind.”</span> He laughs and on cue <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> walks back in, <span style="Color: Pink">his eyes a little red as you piece together he was most likely crying from happiness at being told he was winning a Hero Award. He sees you sitting there and blushes, smiling nervously.</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Alistair",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, hey.”</span> He laughs, rubbing the back of his head, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I guess they did call you in here.”</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You smile back, congratulating <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> on his award, causing him to blush brighter. Guess he is a hero after all.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“St- stop!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> covers his face as he sits down, obviously embarrassed but excited. You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> both laugh at his reaction before you ask why you were called in here. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, the city thinks the awards will mean more if it comes from a member of the community, a peer.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Headmaster Alistair</span> explains, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mostly for symbolic reasons, but it makes a good headline. We asked <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to give them name of a close friend at the school and he mentioned you.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s head snaps up, as if this is news to him as well. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“W- wait! I didn’t know they were going to ask you to give me an award on stage! You- you don’t have to do that!”</span> But you smile and tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> you’d love to be the one to give him the award. <span style="Color: Pink">In fact, you feel pretty honored yourself that he thought of you first.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, yeah… I’ve only known you for a bit but you’re… you know!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> hides his face in his shirt, <span style="Color: Pink">much more shy than usual due to the circumstances.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s award will be the headline at the end of the night, so it would be good for you to be there. The award is meant to celebrate his good deeds, but it can be a little intimidating being on stage like that.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> stands up, patting you both on the shoulder with a smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s parents were made aware of this already and I’ll let <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Dad</span> know, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>. The ceremony is this Saturday at around 6PM. It isn’t a super formal event, but I’d recommend dressing nicely. You are representing the school after all. Maybe come a bit early as well, just so you have time to prepare yourselves.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Alistair</span> stands you both up and leads you back towards the main office. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Feel free to take a minute to process and talk about it, though make sure you get back to class before the bell, okay?”</span> <br>
    <br>
